      "content": "I completely respect your desire for silence and relief from the exhaustion, as withdrawing serves as a valid survival strategy for your mental well-being. While \"opting out\" emotionally is understandable when everything feels too loud, escaping those circumstances entirely often prevents the healing that small, safe steps might eventually offer you. Please consider that while there is no shame in wanting to stop, you're not alone in this struggle, and reaching out to a professional like a therapist could be the one person who truly listens without judgment.",
